mill-proof.logic.r2: argue/answered: U1: answered yes, which keeps mill-proof.logic.r2, to: Does the text's argument take this for granted, whether or not it says so: "if each person's happiness is a good to that person (desirable in the sense of worthy of desire), then the general happiness is a good to the aggregate of all persons"? Answer yes if the author would accept it as part of the argument.
